yond-linux.md\nM\tPOSE.md\nM\tlocales/pt-BR/POSE.md\nM\tpose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/cli/assess.go\nA\tpose-mcp/internal/cli/assess_sealed_test.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/cli/cli.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/cli/cli_test.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go\nA\tpose-mcp/internal/cli/review_reap_test.go\nA\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/assessment_sealed.go\nA\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/assessment_sealed_test.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_list.go\nA\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go\nA\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/engine_reads_raw_history_test.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/integration.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/main_test.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment_regression_test.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_test.go\nA\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusion_local_edits_test.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\nA\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\nA\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux_test.go\nA\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go\nA\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim.go\nA\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go\nA\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_test.go\nA\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_other.go\nA\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows.go\nA\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/review_tree_windows_test.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/pose/testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\nM\tpose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n\n--- KNOWLEDGE SEARCH ---\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:29:The attempt handle remains usable, continuation retains its attempt and ledger, and cancellation does not bypass budgets or create an approval. D4 defers starting tasks over MCP, while resume/handoff of existing tasks are delivered. D3 resolves an authorized unambiguous project using the common project-scope contract.\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-15-decision-log-self-referential-policy-template-contamination.md:89:`validate_orchestration_test.go` (stdio-specific approval diagnostic names\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:53:- Only after an independent approval, pass\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-handoff-pr15-component-aware-review-provenance.md:59:- Do not treat this remediation execution as an approval: the next review\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-routing-round3.md:35:F08 may mislead a user choosing an agent, but does not establish a run proof or approval. F09 would enable fallbacks a caller explicitly disabled if a future writer used the helper on existing schema-2 policy. Neither requires changing the execution, ledger, containment or provenance contracts. R10 remains a shared detector delivery; actual task invocation belongs to pose-delegation-task and is not represented as executed here.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-agency-readiness-outcome-review.md:23:was not used as outcome approval.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-20-handoff-pose-b07-implementation.md:35:3. Review R1 requested changes, now fixed: persisted runs require Git, closeout exceptions require regular materialization, history sorts instants with validated probes. Review R2 found the remaining persisted-materialization gap; Review R3 accepted its correction with no remaining functional finding. The reports record the actual separate same-vendor execution identity. The cross-vendor attempt hit its weekly limit; no cross-vendor approval is claimed.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:27:f-r4-01 is low severity: the deprecated pose review status path omits round/thread fields when constructing interrupted summaries in pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go:611; its text renderer in internal/cli/review_run_continuity.go:116 also omits the round. The current pose delegate ls path and persisted run contain the correct round, and verify/approval do not consume this legacy presentation.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:37:Users of the deprecated status command miss round context; the deprecation hint already points to pose delegate ls. This does not turn partial output into a decision, alter the ledger, or bypass approval. Acceptance is limited to this low-severity presentation gap and its existing replacement.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-13-decision-log-review-assurance-requires-cryptographic-proof.md:18:B01/T2-03 identified different trust paths: the gate checked the signed envelope, while disclosure called an authority checker that only compared claim fields. A claim with coherent fields and a damaged signature could therefore be disclosed as verified although approval was refused. The synthetic regression starts from a trusted valid fixture, damages only the envelope signature, and expects both the verdict and disclosure to refuse verified proof. The old branch has no cryptographic check on the disclosure path; local test execution is unavailable because the Go compiler is truncated.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-13-decision-log-review-assurance-requires-cryptographic-proof.md:22:Verify the stored signature and exact supplied bundle binding inside the shared authority checker. Let the declared path retain its existing signature gate. Keep criteria and decision validation outside authority verification, so a valid proof does not become invalid identity merely because approval fails.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-component-aware-review-plans-review.md:42:invalidate approvals. Keep mapping provenance visible, include only consumed\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
