asons and does not publish.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/mcp-review-attest-integration\",\"rationale\":\"I examined the shared conclusion writer and attestation preflight integration. The change reuses the existing proof and attestation boundary; it adds no provider, consumer or MCP schema.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"I examined the refusal reasons at review_conclusions.go:137-148, 551-563. A currency-only refusal identifies the stale subject and tells the operator to retry after restoring the bundle materialization; no sensitive data is added.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"I examined the public conclude behavior and compatibility documentation. Existing approval behavior and record schemas remain intact; callers gain a non-recorded refusal only for a stale approval, while older run briefs retain versioned verification.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The focused Go command passed. I examined the decision split at review_conclusions.go:125-148, 547-563, proof context at review_run_provenance.go:762-786, and current-bundle admission at review_bundle.go:3158-3173.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-62c2a0e10a1a19a2\",\"rationale\":\"The design assessment observed no structural deltas. D1 implements R1-R2 with the smallest relevant split: a run record and its original brief establish a non-approval, while current bundle currency gates an approval. I examined review_conclusions.go:121-148 and review_run_provenance.go:762-774.\",\"mappings\":[]},\n    {\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"I examined the English and pt-BR manuals and both scaffold copies. Each describes the non-approving local-edit behavior, the approval retry condition and the preserved bundle binding consistently with runtime.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"I examined the returned currency refusal at review_conclusions.go:551-563. It explains that no conclusion was recorded and gives a direct recovery action: make the working tree hold the bundle subject and conclude the same run again.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The focused regression command passed. TestARequestForChangesConcludesOverLocalEdits and TestAnApprovalOverLocalEditsIsNotRecordedAndConcludesLater cover R1-R3 in review_conclusion_local_edits_test.go:41-83; proof, bundle and verdict paths preserve D1.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-62c2a0e10a1a19a2\",\"rationale\":\"I examined all eight sealed subject entries and the implementation. The changes are limited to review conclusion/provenance behavior, regression coverage and the four mirrored manuals; I found no unrelated behavior expansion.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-soundness-residuals-integration\",\"rationale\":\"I examined reviewRunRecordStands and proof verification. A non-approving run remains bound to its recorded bundle, transcript and output; changing its verdict would invalidate the proof, and attestation verification rejects any decision that differs from the run draft. No new authority or input path is introduced.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-62c2a0e10a1a19a2\",\"rationale\":\"I examined D1 and the currency gates at review_conclusions.go:137-148, 551-563. The smallest sufficient choice is to keep run integrity checks universal and apply current-subject checks only to approvals. Always skipping currency could approve stale work; retaining it for all verdicts causes the reported refusal. This choice would be invalidated if a non-approving run could be transformed into an approval or if closeout accepted its old bundle.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-ready artifact-check --spec pose-review-conclude-ignores-local-edits --strict\",\"rationale\":\"The command exited 0. It emitted a large orphan-path report from the broad commit range; the warnings concern unrelated paths and do not affect the scoped subject.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-62c2a0e10a1a19a2\",\"rationale\":\"Ran the JSON assessment; it observed eight subject files and no structural deltas.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-ready assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\"rationale\":\"The no-persist discovery completed and identified the pose-mcp component.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/mcp-review-attest-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The no-persist assessment completed. It reported three unobserved HTTP consumers elsewhere in the repository; they are outside this change, which adds no inter-module contract.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"failed\",\"evidence\":\"command:/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-ready assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"The scan was incomplete: two unrelated existing specs could not be parsed, so the assessment cannot establish repository-wide marker coverage.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"This completion check requires a recorded review attestation. The brief prohibits recording one during this review.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"This completion check requires a recorded review attestation. The brief prohibits recording one during this review.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-ready suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\"rationale\":\"The selector resolved backend-go, security and documentation-style rules, which I applied.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability\",\"rationale\":\"The strict command passed with one target and zero findings; the sealed delivery reachability evidence covers the pose-mcp component.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\"rationale\":\"I ran validate --strict, but the read-only sandbox blocked Go temporary build directories and cache reads before checks executed. The sealed bundle supplies passing build, e2e, integration and unit evidence; the focused regression tests passed locally.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"I ran validate --strict --module pose-mcp, but the read-only sandbox blocked Go temporary build directories and cache reads before checks executed. The sealed pose-mcp evidence supplies passing build, e2e, integration and unit refs; the focused regression tests passed locally.\"}\n  ]\n}\nPOSE_DRAFT'","aggregated_output":"Draft check: the conclusion step would refuse this draft:\n  - the final message carries no pose-draft block\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
